{
  "name": "agama",
  "_about": "SCULPTED (2026-11-08, tools/creaturegen/herps/agama.py): the RAINBOW (red-headed) AGAMA, Agama agama, 28 cm long, the tail 60% of it. A triangular head broad at the jowls and distinct from the neck, cut flat on top and below and sliced back to a blunt snout; a small serrated nuchal crest (a `fin`); a slender depressed trunk carried high on long thin legs, the chest raised, the knees above the hips (more upright than the wall lizard); five long thin toes on each foot (the hind 4th the longest), each with a small curved claw (`horn`); a long round tail lying on the ground, tapering to a whip-thin point; fine keeled scales (`rowscales`). Its walk: the trunk and tail swing side to side (chest, nape against it, the tail's four links a beat apart, faded standing), the legs sweep and lift. Coats: the dominant MALE's breeding dress (base) -- head and nape bright orange-red, body and legs deep indigo blue, the tail blue at its root, then a pale band, orange, a dark tip (the tail one `sweep` along caud1..4, its colour `bands`); the FEMALE -- olive-brown, rows of pale spots down the back, orange patches on the flanks (paints, `when: female`), the tail's bands faint. Variants: male, female, juvenile (.45, the female's dress, paler).",
